2026-09-27T09:47:57.9150562Z Update Note
2026-09-27T09:47:57.9150840Z ===========
2026-09-27T09:47:57.9151246Z Please use this repository instead of ppa:fkrull/deadsnakes.
2026-09-27T09:47:57.9151720Z 
2026-09-27T09:47:57.9151854Z Reporting Issues
2026-09-27T09:47:57.9152152Z ================
2026-09-27T09:47:57.9152335Z 
2026-09-27T09:47:57.9152560Z Issues can be reported in the master issue tracker at:
2026-09-27T09:47:57.9153110Z https://github.com/deadsnakes/issues/issues
2026-09-27T09:47:57.9153445Z 
2026-09-27T09:47:57.9153616Z Supported Ubuntu and Python Versions
2026-09-27T09:47:57.9154017Z ====================================
2026-09-27T09:47:57.9154278Z 
2026-09-27T09:47:57.9154490Z - Ubuntu 22.04 (jammy) Python3.7+ (NOT Python3.10)
2026-09-27T09:47:57.9155462Z - Ubuntu 24.04 (noble) Python3.7+ (NOT Python3.12)
2026-09-27T09:47:57.9156251Z - Ubuntu 26.04 (resolute) Python3.7+ (NOT Python3.14)
2026-09-27T09:47:57.9157269Z - Note: Python 3.10 (jammy), Python3.12 (noble), Python3.14 (resolute) are not provided by deadsnakes as upstream ubuntu provides those packages.
2026-09-27T09:47:57.9158228Z 
2026-09-27T09:47:57.9158381Z Why some packages aren't built:
2026-09-27T09:47:57.9159049Z - Note: for 22.04+, older python versions requre libssl<3 so they are not currently built
2026-09-27T09:47:57.9159974Z - If you need these, reach out to asottile to set up a private ppa
2026-09-27T09:47:57.9160447Z 
2026-09-27T09:47:57.9160970Z The packages may also work on other versions of Ubuntu or Debian, but that is not tested or supported.
2026-09-27T09:47:57.9161658Z 
2026-09-27T09:47:57.9161805Z Packages
2026-09-27T09:47:57.9162090Z ========
2026-09-27T09:47:57.9247620Z 
2026-09-27T09:47:57.9249836Z The packages provided here are loosely based on the debian upstream packages with some modifications to make them more usable as non-default pythons and on ubuntu.  As such, the packages follow debian's patterns and often do not include a full python distribution with just `apt install python#.#`.  Here is a list of packages that may be useful along with the default install:
2026-09-27T09:47:57.9252036Z 
2026-09-27T09:47:57.9252392Z - `python#.#-dev`: includes development headers for building C extensions
2026-09-27T09:47:57.9253129Z - `python#.#-venv`: provides the standard library `venv` module
2026-09-27T09:47:57.9254237Z - `python#.#-distutils`: provides the standard library `distutils` module
2026-09-27T09:47:57.9255153Z - `python#.#-lib2to3`: provides the `2to3-#.#` utility as well as the standard library `lib2to3` module
2026-09-27T09:47:57.9256253Z - `python#.#-gdbm`: provides the standard library `dbm.gnu` module
2026-09-27T09:47:57.9256920Z - `python#.#-tk`: provides the standard library `tkinter` module
2026-09-27T09:47:57.9257562Z 
2026-09-27T09:47:57.9257722Z Third-Party Python Modules
2026-09-27T09:47:57.9258084Z ==========================
2026-09-27T09:47:57.9258320Z 
2026-09-27T09:47:57.9260013Z Python modules in the official Ubuntu repositories are packaged to work with the Python interpreters from the official repositories. Accordingly, they generally won't work with the Python interpreters from this PPA. As an exception, pure-Python modules for Python 3 will work, but any compiled extension modules won't.
2026-09-27T09:47:57.9261842Z 
2026-09-27T09:47:57.9262861Z To install 3rd-party Python modules, you should use the common Python packaging tools.  For an introduction into the Python packaging ecosystem and its tools, refer to the Python Packaging User Guide:
2026-09-27T09:47:57.9264267Z https://packaging.python.org/installing/
2026-09-27T09:47:57.9264621Z 
